{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/ml07i9sv","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":72.96,"top":196.8,"width":528,"height":124.8},"name":"Text 4","text":"Flat fit over about 2.4 orders of magnitude. Scale is collinear with the recipe. Single-seed anchors.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":20,"typeface":"Calibri","color":"#3F3A36","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/oryp8fah","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":682.56,"top":134.4,"width":528,"height":48},"name":"Text 6","text":"No length-bias finding","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":26.67,"typeface":"Georgia","color":"#8C3A2F","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/pc76hkr2","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":682.56,"top":196.8,"width":528,"height":124.8},"name":"Text 7","text":"In the controlled comparison, completion length drifts shorter. GRPO and Dr. GRPO are indistinguishable on held-out gain.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":20,"typeface":"Calibri","color":"#3F3A36","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/w32twb6l","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":72.96,"top":398.4,"width":528,"height":48},"name":"Text 9","text":"No group-size optimum","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":26.67,"typeface":"Georgia","color":"#8C3A2F","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/v2tcn650","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":72.96,"top":460.8,"width":528,"height":124.8},"name":"Text 10","text":"G = 2 through 16 are not separable on the three-seed sweep. G = 16 versus G = 2 fails equivalence at ±0.02 (TOST p = 0.056).","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":20,"typeface":"Calibri","color":"#3F3A36","alignment":"left"}}
